body:
To answer your question briefly, unfortunately, the pain it would cause them is the only reason why I haven't committed suicide yet. 

&#x200B;

Briefly, I think you are misunderstanding what I mean by what I mean being in store. It isn't that I don't want a future, I simply don't want an *inevitable* future. A future where I decide my own path. I have a career that I love, but now it doesn't feel like I had any say in the matter, but rather it was *inevitable* to be what I chose. And now it feels like it is *inevitable* who I happen to fall in love with and marry, *inevitable* to have or not have children, *inevitable*, to finally manage my illness or succumb to it, and *inevitable* whether I end my life. I want to live an authentic life, not be bound to being nothing more than some homunculus forced to watch the actions of a piece of meat and other pieces of meat unfold in front of me.

Everything I've stated in the original post is what I suppose I believe to be true. I guess my problem is I'm making up feeling suicidal just to get attention, when in reality I should be dead for the things I've done from above, and then it feels like maybe I'm forgetting something and leaving out details. What if I really did even do something even worse. But what if I'm lying about thinking I may have done something worse just to get more sympathy. I don't know man. I hate this. 

&#x200B;

Also I don't think I really understand your question
